Hmm, no, i don't think you can teleport _from the dungeons of doom
(DoD) into the quest_ with anything other than the Eye of the
Aethiopica's invocation. It seems that having been granted permission
by the quest leader is already sufficient - the leader being angry
with you in and of itself doesn't prevent you from using the stairs in
debug mode, as long as the level and alignment requirements are met.

Oh, and if you somehow manage to appease your quest leader (a scroll
of taming, read while confused would probably be best), you _might_
get allowed on the quest after all; don't know for sure, but Neferet
the Green returned to talking normally to my testing character (who
acquired the Eye from a debug-mode-wish, or she wouldn't have been
able to get back to the Quest branch).

> >So, getting thrown out of the quest for good will only make the game
> >unwinnable if you've not yet gone below the start level and/or if your
> >role is wizard.
> 
> and/or?  :)

I think an "or" might be misconstrued as being meant exclusively,
leaving out characters who fulfil both conditions.

